course: dictionary
lesson: 11309
title: Yell: a loud shout
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To yell means to shout something very loudly. People yell when they are angry, excited, scared or in pain, or to call someone who is far away. A yell is the loud shout itself.
explain: Read the words around yell to see why someone is doing it. «If someone tries to grab you, yell loudly «No!»» The clue is grab: the yell is loud so that people nearby can hear and help.
explain: Yelling has a time and a place. It can save lives, but at home, at school and with people, we do not yell, because it can scare or upset them. Mum in Liverpool might yell, «Clean your room, it's a tip!», but that is a loud reminder, not a sweet whisper.
fact: Yell can be a verb (yell, yells, yelled, yelling) or a noun: a yell is a loud shout.
fact: «Yell» means to shout very loudly, because you are angry, excited, scared or in pain, or to call someone far away.
fact: «Yell for help» means to shout loudly so that someone comes to help you.
fact: «Let out a yell» means to make a loud shout.
fact: In safety, a loud «No! Go! Tell!» can warn people when a stranger tries to grab you.
exercise: «If someone tries to grab you, yell loudly «No!»» What does yell mean here? | *To shout very loudly | To whisper quietly | To walk away slowly | To sing a happy tune
exercise: Which phrase means to shout loudly to get someone to come and help you? | yell at the dog | *yell for help | whisper softly | sit very still
exercise: Why should we not yell indoors or at people? | *Because it can scare or upset them | Because it helps us think faster | Because yelling is always quiet | Because the walls need to hear it
test: Yesterday Leo ___ at the fan when it exploded. | yells | yelling | *yelled | yell
test: Which reasons can make a person yell? | Because they are reading a book quietly | Because they are bored and sleepy | *Because they are angry, excited, scared or in pain | Because they want to whisper a secret
exam: Which sentence shows a safe use of yell? | Yell at your sister during library time | Yell quietly and softly at the bus stop | Yell at the dog and then at your friends | *If a stranger tries to grab you, yell «No!»
